  "rationale": "The ascension win condition changed on purpose, and this is the only committed gate that can observe it. Both paths now require positive achievement: Path A counts permitted cells standing at their floor (ascension-summit-cells 13, ascension-summit-copies 2) and Path B requires each era boundary to hold a canon of ascension-canon-breadth 77 nodes spanning ascension-canon-cells 18 distinct cells, with a scale-relative loss allowance (ascension-loss-fraction 51, floored by the authored ascension-loss-max 2). No authored constant changed value. Measured at n=96 over 2400 ticks: ascensionRate fell 0.771 to 0.125, inside the 0.05-0.20 band; the exploit margin against uniform-random-legal went -0.229 to +0.125; correlation between per-strategy ascension rate and mean nodes known rose 0.324 to 0.957. The reference metrics move because seven of the eight strategies now run to the tick cap instead of ascending around tick 700-1200, so their census is taken at 2400 ticks rather than at the tick they stopped. The 60-tick and 240-tick gates were regenerated in the same change and no metric moved in either, which is the evidence that this movement is the win condition and not a simulation change.",
